// Title: Suspicious Processes Spawned by Java.EXE
// Sigma ID: 0d34ed8b-1c12-4ff2-828c-16fc860b766d
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Andreas Hunkeler (@Karneades), Florian Roth
// Date: 2021-12-17 | Modified: 2024-01-18
// ATT&CK: initial-access, persistence, privilege-escalation
// Description: Detects suspicious processes spawned from a Java host process which could indicate a sign of
//   exploitation (e.g. log4j)
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate calls to system binaries
//   - Company specific internal usage
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20231230220738/https://www.lunasec.io/docs/blog/log4j-zero-day/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_java_susp_child_process.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\java.exe" and (FolderPath endswith "\\AppVLP.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\bitsadmin.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\certutil.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\cscript.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\curl.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\forfiles.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\hh.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\mftrace.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\mshta.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\net.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\net1.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\query.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\reg.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\regsvr32.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\rundll32.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\schtasks.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\scrcons.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\scriptrunner.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\sh.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\systeminfo.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\whoami.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\wmic.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\wscript.exe")
